{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>Who then is he?</b> If you are Esav, who was it that brought me game? For the word אֵיפוֹא, with an alef at the end of the word, serves in the sense of 'if so'; but the word אֵיפֹה, with a heh at the end, serves in the sense of 'where,' as in: אֵיפֹה הֵם רֹעִים (Genesis 37:16)." "<b>He too shall be blessed.</b> If so, who is he that brought me game through deception and will thereby also merit being blessed? For he perceived through his blessing that the blessing had taken effect upon the one blessed, as they said of Rabbi Ḥanina when he would pray for the sick (Berakhot 34a)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:01.830092301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}